3. **OAuth provider integration**: Spring Security supports OAuth integration using the `@EnableOAuth2Sso` annotation. Here is a simple example for Google login:

```java
@Configuration
public class SecurityConfig extends WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter {
    @Override
    protected void configure(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        http
            .antMatcher(""/**"").authorizeRequests()
                .antMatchers(""/"", ""/login**"", ""/webjars/**"", ""/error**"") // permit these URLs without authentication
                .permitAll()
            .anyRequest()
                .authenticated()
            .and().exceptionHandling()
                .accessDeniedPage(""/403"") // handle access denied exception here
            .and().logout().logoutSuccessUrl(""/"").permitAll() // log out URL configuration
            .and()
            .oauth2Login()

